# Optional recipe-source API keys
# --------------------------------
# The app works with NO keys (TheMealDB + a category fallback). Add keys to a
# real local `.env` file (Vite auto-loads `.env`, which is gitignored) to enable
# the larger / more region-aware recipe sources. Never commit a real key — only
# this `.env.example` template is tracked.

# --- Spoonacular (2nd source, larger) --------------------------------------
# Register for a free key at https://spoonacular.com
# VITE_SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=your-spoonacular-key

# --- Edamam (3rd source, best regional coverage) ---------------------------
# NOTE: Edamam's Recipe API is PAID only — there is no free tier (plans start
# around $9/mo, 10-day trial on some plans). Only add these if you intend to
# pay. If unset, the app silently skips Edamam and uses the free sources.
# VITE_EDAMAM_APP_ID=your-edamam-app-id
# VITE_EDAMAM_APP_KEY=your-edamam-app-key

# --- DeepSeek (optional AI recipe suggestions) -----------------------------
# PAID (cheap), no free tier. Get a key at https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
# When set, the app asks the model for a random, region-appropriate dish and
# adds it to the pool (clearly marked "suggested by AI"). Instructions are
# AI-written, not verified — the real verified recipes remain primary.
# VITE_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your-deepseek-key
# VITE_DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# --- Server storage & backups (read by server.mjs when deployed) ----------
# Where the live saved-recipes file lives, and where timestamped backups go.
# Both default to folders inside the repo (data/ and backup/); you can point
# them somewhere external, e.g. a OneDrive-synced or drive-backed folder.
# CQ_DATA_DIR=folder  for favorites.json              (default: data)
# CQ_BACKUP_DIR=folder for timestamped backups         (default: backup)
# CQ_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MS=how often to auto-backup       (default: 6h i.e. 21600000)


